SUMMARY:T.C. Steele – Indiana’s Master Impressionist from Munich to Brown County
DESCRIPTION:This is the Largest Exhibition of T.C. Steele’s Work in 100 Years! The exhibit is open to public starting at Noon on July 19th, followed by a special presentation of “Selma and the Painter” starring Jill Tasker at 2:00 pm. Free admission all day and $25 Souvenir Catalogue. The exhibit will then be ongoing during regular operating hours through September 20th with free admission and free parking.\n
