SUMMARY:T.C. Steele Memorial Exhibition
DESCRIPTION:The T.C. Steele Memorial Exhibition at the Brown County Art Guild commemorates the 100th anniversary of Steele’s passing and honors his enduring artistic legacy in Brown County from 1907 to 1926. This special exhibition features a remarkable collection of landscapes, floral still lifes, and portraiture from regional museums, public libraries, and private collections—celebrating the beauty, light, and spirit that inspired one of Indiana’s most beloved painters.\n\nJuly 3rd- September 4th 2026\n—————————————————————————————–\nBrown County Art Guild – A not for profit organization located in the heart of downtown Nashville, Indiana.  On display throughout its galleries is a prized collection of historic paintings as well as current works for sale from regional award-winning member artists.  The Guild also offers artist demonstrations, workshops, and a variety of events or programs throughout the year.\nVisit our website: browncountyartguild.org or call 812-9088-6185 for more information   \nHours: March – December, Monday – Saturday 11am-5pm & Sundays 12-4pm\nWinter Hours: January & February, Thursday – Saturday 11am-5pm & Sundays 12-4pm\n
