TRANSP:OPAQUE
SUMMARY:The Texas Tenors
DESCRIPTION:Billboard #1 Recording Artists, 3-time Emmy Award Winners & 2022 Texas Country Music Hall of Fame Inductees THE TEXAS TENORS are coming to the Brown County Music Center!\nSince appearing on America’s Got Talent in 2009, The Texas Tenors (JC Fisher, Marcus Collins and John Hagen) have released five studio albums, three PBS Specials, five DVDs, multiple singles and two children’s books that have earned them impressive recognition including three Emmy Awards, The Gelett Burgess Award for Excellence in Children’s Literature and the distinction of being Billboard Magazine’s #10 Classical Artist in the World. The Texas Tenors are the most successful music group and third highest selling artist in the history of America’s Got Talent. \nThe group’s most recent albums “Outside the Lines,” “Rise,” and “A Collection of Broadway and American Classics” all debuted at No. 1 on the Billboard Charts. These classically trained, versatile tenors have performed more than 2,500 concerts around the world including headline shows in Las Vegas, China and a 24-city tour of the United Kingdom. The show will feature music from their latest album along with rousing patriotic favorites and everything from country to classical.\n
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/the-texas-tenors/
CATEGORIES:Entertainment,Happening,Live Music,Theatre &amp; Entertainment
