SUMMARY:Debutants with special guest The Hammer and The Hatchet
DESCRIPTION:Debutants is a seven-piece “Indiana Newgrass” band from Fort Wayne, Indiana, crafting vibrant, genre-defying music rooted in bluegrass instrumentation and driven by a wide-ranging love of indie folk, Americana, and improvisational music. With guitar, mandolin, banjo, two fiddles, cello, and upright bass, their sound nods to tradition while confidently stepping beyond it—honoring the past without being bound by it.\nDebutants thrives in the space between structure and spontaneity. Their original songs are thoughtfully arranged as a group—catchy, earnest, and intriguing—reflecting the band’s collaborative spirit and diverse musical voices. With five songwriters and six singers contributing up to six-part harmonies, Debutants offers a constantly shifting yet cohesive sound. Onstage, the band’s chemistry is undeniable: joyful, energetic, and deeply connected. The best compliment they’ve received—being described as “one big musical amoeba”—captures their essence perfectly: distinct parts moving together as one living, breathing organism.\nAbove all, Debutants plays music that feels alive. Their performances radiate positivity, connection, and genuine love for one another—and that joy is contagious, leaving audiences energized, smiling, and fully in the moment.\nWITH SPECIAL GUEST THE HAMMER AND THE HATCHET\n
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/debutants-with-special-guest-the-hammer-and-the-hatchet/
CATEGORIES:Entertainment,Family Friendly,Happening,Live Music,Theatre &amp; Entertainment
LOCATION:Brown County Playhouse, South Van Buren Street, Nashville, IN
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/playhouse82011.jpg
